WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.203
- All right so how did
you get started, Marie?

00:00:02.203 --> 00:00:04.490
Like with tidying up, this whole thing.

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:08.124
(speaks Japanese)

00:00:08.124 --> 00:00:09.029
- So I actually,

00:00:09.029 --> 00:00:11.084
became very interested
in the art of tidying

00:00:11.084 --> 00:00:12.001
at the age five.

00:00:12.001 --> 00:00:14.834
(speaks Japanese)

00:00:20.094 --> 00:00:22.590
And I was just very interested
in organizing things.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.970
So I would organize my
family's items secretly,

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:26.676
and I would get in trouble for that.

00:00:26.676 --> 00:00:27.640
(audience laughs)

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.473
- What?

00:00:28.473 --> 00:00:29.306
You got in trouble?

00:00:29.306 --> 00:00:31.808
I would pay my children to tidy up.

00:00:31.808 --> 00:00:34.316
My five year old never does that.

00:00:34.316 --> 00:00:37.149
(speaks Japanese)

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:46.947
- So after a lot of (mumbles),

00:00:46.947 --> 00:00:49.211
but of course that was kind
of part of the process.

00:00:49.211 --> 00:00:50.837
And at the age of 19 that's when I decided

00:00:50.837 --> 00:00:54.796
to turn this organizational
tidying thing into my business.

00:00:54.796 --> 00:00:55.629
- A beast, yeah.

00:00:55.629 --> 00:00:57.083
Everyone's in.

00:00:57.083 --> 00:01:00.543
So how does being tidy help
in other areas of your life?

00:01:00.543 --> 00:01:03.376
(speaks Japanese)

00:01:07.184 --> 00:01:08.856
- So I feel like when
you tidy something up,

00:01:08.856 --> 00:01:10.226
you're not just tidying up your house,

00:01:10.226 --> 00:01:12.722
it really kind of tidies up
your mind and your heart as well

00:01:12.722 --> 00:01:14.228
(speaks Japanese)

00:01:14.228 --> 00:01:15.682
- That's my issue.

00:01:15.682 --> 00:01:18.515
(speaks Japanese)

00:01:27.175 --> 00:01:29.161
- So through the tidying up process,

00:01:29.161 --> 00:01:32.284
it kind of teaches yourself
what sparks joy in you,

00:01:32.284 --> 00:01:34.339
and then once you kind
of train this muscle,

00:01:34.339 --> 00:01:37.254
you can apply that to other
areas of your life as well.

00:01:37.254 --> 00:01:38.507
- I'm in.

00:01:38.507 --> 00:01:39.755
I need it.

00:01:39.755 --> 00:01:41.596
(laughs)

00:01:41.596 --> 00:01:44.127
So what's your process
of getting rid of things?

00:01:44.127 --> 00:01:46.960
(speaks Japanese)

00:01:53.148 --> 00:01:55.528
- The most important thing
is to organize and tidy

00:01:55.528 --> 00:01:56.361
by category,

00:01:56.361 --> 00:01:57.559
and the first step in doing so

00:01:57.559 --> 00:02:00.221
is you have to take all the
items from that category

00:02:00.221 --> 00:02:02.064
and collect them in a single space.

00:02:02.064 --> 00:02:03.372
- [Kelly] Oh gosh.

00:02:03.372 --> 00:02:06.705
(Marie speaks Japanese)

00:02:08.786 --> 00:02:10.151
- So if you're gonna start with clothes,

00:02:10.151 --> 00:02:13.244
then get every single article
of clothing in your house

00:02:13.244 --> 00:02:15.968
in one space and you grab it,
you touch it, you feel it,

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.119
and you see if it sparks
joy inside of you.

00:02:18.119 --> 00:02:19.543
- [Kelly] Is there anything you've had

00:02:19.543 --> 00:02:21.366
a hard time letting go of?

00:02:21.366 --> 00:02:24.699
(Marie speaks Japanese)

00:02:31.681 --> 00:02:36.348
- So there's actually a t-shirt
that I purchased in 2005,

00:02:36.348 --> 00:02:39.114
a long time ago that I
just can't get rid of.

00:02:39.114 --> 00:02:40.234
- [Audience] Awww.
(laughs)

00:02:40.234 --> 00:02:42.207
- [Kelly] It's so clean.

00:02:42.207 --> 00:02:43.265
From 2005?

00:02:43.265 --> 00:02:44.198
No stains?

00:02:44.198 --> 00:02:45.031
What?

00:02:45.985 --> 00:02:47.320
(speaks Japanese)

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:48.941
- Someone owns a Tide pen.

00:02:48.941 --> 00:02:51.449
(laughs)

00:02:51.449 --> 00:02:54.782
(Marie speaks Japanese)

00:02:57.084 --> 00:02:57.917
- It's a little embarrassing,

00:02:57.917 --> 00:02:58.756
and I can't explain why,

00:02:58.756 --> 00:03:01.043
but it just sparks so
much joy inside of me.

00:03:01.043 --> 00:03:03.084
And this is the first time
that I'm showing it on TV.

00:03:03.084 --> 00:03:04.109
(audience laughs)

00:03:04.109 --> 00:03:05.250
- You know what would spark joy in me,

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.367
if I could fit in it.

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:09.200
(audience laughs)

00:03:10.344 --> 00:03:12.769
Anything that you're
still holding onto, Seth?

00:03:12.769 --> 00:03:15.776
- I have a shirt I bought in college

00:03:15.776 --> 00:03:19.432
that is a Bacardi rum shirt
that I found in a thrift store.

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:20.267
(audience laughs)

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:21.391
And there it is.

00:03:21.391 --> 00:03:22.224
And it says,

00:03:22.224 --> 00:03:23.938
"I'm rich, smooth, and flavorful."

00:03:23.938 --> 00:03:26.724
And I've had it for 20+ years,

00:03:26.724 --> 00:03:28.818
and I'm happy every time I see it.

00:03:28.818 --> 00:03:29.651
(audience laughs)

00:03:29.651 --> 00:03:31.809
- I was gonna say, "I don't
know, that sparks joy for me,

00:03:31.809 --> 00:03:33.072
and it's not even mine."

00:03:33.072 --> 00:03:33.905
(audience laughs)

00:03:33.905 --> 00:03:36.053
Especially seeing your kid
hold up a Bacardi shirt.

00:03:36.053 --> 00:03:37.286
(audience laughs)

00:03:37.286 --> 00:03:39.938
- Also let's note the absence
of joy in my son's face.

00:03:39.938 --> 00:03:41.004
(audience laughs)
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:41.004 --> 00:03:42.196
It's like, "Fine, dad."

00:03:42.196 --> 00:03:44.255
- [Seth] It's sparking nothing.

00:03:44.255 --> 00:03:45.126
- So Marie,

00:03:45.126 --> 00:03:46.960
you just released your first kids book.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.793
What is "Kiki &amp; Jax" about?

00:03:48.793 --> 00:03:51.626
(speaks Japanese)

00:03:54.007 --> 00:03:55.261
- So I actually created this book

00:03:55.261 --> 00:03:58.395
because I wanted to kind of
convey the joy of tidying up

00:03:58.395 --> 00:03:59.847
to the younger generation.

00:03:59.847 --> 00:04:02.680
(speaks Japanese)

00:04:05.733 --> 00:04:07.405
And it's not just an instructional book

00:04:07.405 --> 00:04:08.276
that teaches kids,

00:04:08.276 --> 00:04:09.437
"This is how you tidy."

00:04:09.437 --> 00:04:11.236
It's actually a story, a narrative about

00:04:11.236 --> 00:04:13.245
how the two's friendship is kind of

00:04:13.245 --> 00:04:15.497
based on this idea of tidying.

00:04:15.497 --> 00:04:17.656
- Okay. I'm gonna take that home.

00:04:17.656 --> 00:04:18.701
(audience laughs)

00:04:18.701 --> 00:04:21.209
To read to my children.

00:04:21.209 --> 00:04:23.018
All of them.

00:04:23.018 --> 00:04:25.882
Even the teenagers.
(laughs)

00:04:25.882 --> 00:04:29.924
Marie's new children's book,
"Kiki &amp; Jax" is out now.

00:04:29.924 --> 00:04:31.344
- [Beth] I'm obsessed with Marie Kondo

00:04:31.344 --> 00:04:35.721
and the spark joy
decluttering extravaganza

00:04:35.721 --> 00:04:37.138
that has taken over America.

00:04:37.138 --> 00:04:38.466
- And in case you don't know her...

00:04:38.466 --> 00:04:39.924
You pick things, right?

00:04:39.924 --> 00:04:40.973
In your house?

00:04:40.973 --> 00:04:41.806
- [Beth] Yes.

00:04:41.806 --> 00:04:42.982
And you make sure that
they spark joy to you.

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:43.980
She has a whole thing, look,

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:44.813
I've read the book,

00:04:44.813 --> 00:04:45.646
I've highlighted,

00:04:45.646 --> 00:04:47.603
I've done every room in
my house but the garage,

00:04:47.603 --> 00:04:50.442
and it's now this amazing sanctuary.

00:04:50.442 --> 00:04:51.275
- [Kelly] So you feel better?

00:04:51.275 --> 00:04:52.111
- I feel clearer.

00:04:52.111 --> 00:04:52.947
I have more time.

00:04:52.947 --> 00:04:53.783
It's amazing.

00:04:53.783 --> 00:04:55.664
I'm like full-blown Marie Kondo,

00:04:55.664 --> 00:04:57.330
like, bow down.
(laughs)

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.163
(audience laughs)

00:04:58.163 --> 00:04:59.286
- All right, y'all.
(audience cheers and applause)

00:04:59.286 --> 00:05:00.621
Please welcome Beth Behrs.

00:05:00.621 --> 00:05:05.288
(soulful instrumental music)
(audience cheers and applause)

00:05:05.288 --> 00:05:06.380
- Hi!

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:07.213
Oh my god!

00:05:07.213 --> 00:05:08.046
Hi!

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:10.413
- [Kelly] Meet Seth.

00:05:10.413 --> 00:05:11.246
- [Beth] I can't believe I'm here.

00:05:11.246 --> 00:05:12.214
- [Beth] Hi Seth!

00:05:12.214 --> 00:05:13.047
- [Seth] Hi Beth!
How are you?

00:05:13.047 --> 00:05:13.880
It's good to see you.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:14.746
- [Beth] Hi Kelly!
- [Kelly] Hi!

00:05:14.746 --> 00:05:16.249
- [Kelly] I was so excited
you could come back!

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:17.089
(Beth claps)

00:05:17.089 --> 00:05:20.604
- I have met so many actresses
and celebrities I love,

00:05:20.604 --> 00:05:22.693
but you're my favorite ever.

00:05:22.693 --> 00:05:23.526
(audience cheers)

00:05:23.526 --> 00:05:24.888
- [Marie] Thank you.
- [Beth] I love you so much!

00:05:24.888 --> 00:05:25.774
- [Marie] Thank you.

00:05:25.774 --> 00:05:26.607
- Okay.

00:05:26.607 --> 00:05:27.982
Marie, this is Beth,

00:05:27.982 --> 00:05:29.021
and I swear she won't harm you.

00:05:29.021 --> 00:05:29.854
- [Beth] I swear.

00:05:29.854 --> 00:05:30.687
I mean, we'll see.
(laughs)

00:05:30.687 --> 00:05:31.520
I don't know.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:32.655
- [Kelly] Just kidding.
(laughs)

00:05:32.655 --> 00:05:33.897
Is there anything that you
would want to say to Marie?

00:05:33.897 --> 00:05:34.730
That's why we had you here.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:35.563
We were like, "You gotta have a question."

00:05:35.563 --> 00:05:36.396
- [Beth] Yes.

00:05:36.396 --> 00:05:38.421
No, just thank you so much.

00:05:38.421 --> 00:05:39.326
You say in your book,

00:05:39.326 --> 00:05:40.159
and it's so true,

00:05:40.159 --> 00:05:41.481
that it goes beyond decluttering.

00:05:41.481 --> 00:05:43.208
Like, it really changes your whole life,

00:05:43.208 --> 00:05:44.996
and I've had so much, like...

00:05:44.996 --> 00:05:46.134
people walk into my house and be like,

00:05:46.134 --> 00:05:47.794
"There's just a different energy in here.

00:05:47.794 --> 00:05:49.408
Like, it just feels better."
- [Marie] Oh.

00:05:49.408 --> 00:05:50.673
And I feel better,

00:05:50.673 --> 00:05:52.461
and everybody should do it.
(laughs)

00:05:52.461 --> 00:05:54.423
(audience cheers and applause)

00:05:54.423 --> 00:05:55.256
- [Marie] Thank you.

00:05:55.256 --> 00:05:56.174
Thank you so much.

00:05:56.174 --> 00:05:57.059
I'm so happy.
(laughs)

00:05:57.059 --> 00:05:59.927
- [Kelly] Beth used the KonMari
Method on her whole house.

00:05:59.927 --> 00:06:01.645
We have some photos, let's see 'em.

00:06:01.645 --> 00:06:02.478
- [Audience] Whoa!

00:06:02.478 --> 00:06:03.311
- [Kelly] Look at those piles.

00:06:03.311 --> 00:06:04.385
- [Marie] Wow!
(laughs)

00:06:04.385 --> 00:06:05.813
- [Beth] Obviously that was the closet.

00:06:05.813 --> 00:06:06.646
(audience laughs)

00:06:06.646 --> 00:06:07.479
Yeah, this many.

00:06:07.479 --> 00:06:09.161
- [Kelly] That's her
dog amongst the things.

00:06:09.161 --> 00:06:10.003
- [Audience] Whoa!

00:06:10.003 --> 00:06:11.427
- [Kelly] Okay, okay.

00:06:11.427 --> 00:06:12.907
It's getting better, getting better.

00:06:12.907 --> 00:06:13.893
I fold, I roll like that.

00:06:13.893 --> 00:06:16.643
- [Beth] So I have a tiny closet,

00:06:17.493 --> 00:06:19.780
but that's the most room
I've ever had in it,

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:22.078
and I'm very proud of that.
(laughs)

00:06:22.078 --> 00:06:24.056
- [Kelly] Dude, that was a
lot of clothes on the floor.

00:06:24.056 --> 00:06:24.889
- [Beth] There was a lot.

00:06:24.889 --> 00:06:26.278
- [Kelly] So how did Beth do?

00:06:26.278 --> 00:06:27.544
(speaks Japanese)

00:06:27.544 --> 00:06:28.673
- [Marie] Excellent.
(laughs)

00:06:28.673 --> 00:06:29.506
- [Beth] Yay!

00:06:29.506 --> 00:06:30.542
- [Kelly] All right.

00:06:30.542 --> 00:06:32.667
Well, Beth do you have any
more questions for Marie?

00:06:32.667 --> 00:06:34.048
Like, you said you have a tiny closet.

00:06:34.048 --> 00:06:34.966
Is there anything?

00:06:34.966 --> 00:06:35.799
- [Beth] Yeah.

00:06:35.799 --> 00:06:36.881
So I have a tiny closet,

00:06:36.881 --> 00:06:39.726
and I got rid of anything
that didn't spark joy,

00:06:39.726 --> 00:06:42.431
but then I got some new
clothes that did spark joy.

00:06:42.431 --> 00:06:44.567
(laughs)

00:06:44.567 --> 00:06:45.400
And so,

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:48.021
now my closet doesn't
look like that anymore.

00:06:48.021 --> 00:06:49.519
(laughs)

00:06:49.519 --> 00:06:50.691
And I don't know why.

00:06:50.691 --> 00:06:51.574
I miss that it...

00:06:51.574 --> 00:06:52.688
It looked so good,

00:06:52.688 --> 00:06:55.115
and now it looks more cluttered and,

00:06:55.115 --> 00:06:56.612
can you help me?
(laughs)

00:06:56.612 --> 00:06:59.445
(speaks Japanese)

00:07:05.413 --> 00:07:06.411
- [Translator] So just understanding

00:07:06.411 --> 00:07:08.083
the folding process very thoroughly,

00:07:08.083 --> 00:07:11.171
that really kind of saves a lot
of space inside your closet.

00:07:11.171 --> 00:07:12.286
- [Beth] Oh. Okay.

00:07:12.286 --> 00:07:13.749
I didn't even think about that.

00:07:13.749 --> 00:07:14.619
Like, folding it, yeah,

00:07:14.619 --> 00:07:15.850
and shelves like that.

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:17.300
- [Kelly] Wait, well
aren't we about to learn

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:18.335
how to fold it properly?

00:07:18.335 --> 00:07:19.168
Right?

00:07:19.168 --> 00:07:20.751
(translates to Japanese)

00:07:20.751 --> 00:07:21.584
I think so.

00:07:21.584 --> 00:07:22.417
- [Beth] Yeah.

00:07:22.417 --> 00:07:24.051
- [Kelly] You get the
"Kelly Clarkson Show" shirt.

00:07:24.051 --> 00:07:24.933
- [Beth] This is good
too because I have a lot-

00:07:24.933 --> 00:07:25.850
- [Kelly] You love Kelly-

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:27.395
- [Beth] I love Kelly Clarkson.

00:07:27.395 --> 00:07:29.310
I have a lot of problems
with the (mumbles).

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:33.187
I always do it upside down
where you can't see the t-shirt.

00:07:33.187 --> 00:07:35.196
I forget how to do it the
way you're supposed to.

00:07:35.196 --> 00:07:36.531
- [Kelly] I worked a bit in apparel,

00:07:36.531 --> 00:07:37.994
so you can usually see my...

00:07:37.994 --> 00:07:39.619
I had a lot of jobs.
(laughs)

00:07:39.619 --> 00:07:42.452
(speaks Japanese)

00:07:43.485 --> 00:07:45.023
- Yeah so if you want to show the logo,

00:07:45.023 --> 00:07:47.159
just make sure when you
start it's on the outside,

00:07:47.159 --> 00:07:48.331
it's facing you.

00:07:48.331 --> 00:07:49.164
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:07:49.164 --> 00:07:50.003
- [Beth] Oh, facing.

00:07:50.003 --> 00:07:50.836
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:07:50.836 --> 00:07:51.669
So wait,

00:07:51.669 --> 00:07:52.502
this is wrong?

00:07:52.502 --> 00:07:53.335
This is wrong?

00:07:53.335 --> 00:07:54.206
You shouldn't do this?

00:07:54.206 --> 00:07:57.039
(speaks Japanese)

00:07:58.659 --> 00:07:59.492
- [Translator] Oh, so you flip it over.

00:07:59.492 --> 00:08:00.325
- [Beth] Oh.

00:08:00.325 --> 00:08:01.158
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:08:01.158 --> 00:08:01.991
- [Kelly] Gosh, Seth.

00:08:01.991 --> 00:08:02.824
You're so wrong.

00:08:02.824 --> 00:08:05.398
- I'm doing good.
(audience laughs)

00:08:05.398 --> 00:08:07.767
- [Kelly] I love that you have
a shirt for like a mini Seth.

00:08:07.767 --> 00:08:09.850
(laughs)

00:08:11.099 --> 00:08:11.981
- So how do you do it?

00:08:11.981 --> 00:08:12.852
You fold this in?

00:08:12.852 --> 00:08:15.036
(speaks Japanese)

00:08:15.036 --> 00:08:15.869
- [Beth] Oh my god,

00:08:15.869 --> 00:08:16.835
we're folding with Marie Kondo.

00:08:16.835 --> 00:08:17.668
- [Kelly] I know.
(audience cheers)

00:08:17.668 --> 00:08:19.251
I'm in, I'm in.

00:08:19.251 --> 00:08:21.453
Okay, this is like the
proper way to get in there.

00:08:21.453 --> 00:08:22.286
- [Translator] And of course,

00:08:22.286 --> 00:08:23.821
make sure you pour in
some love as you do this.

00:08:23.821 --> 00:08:24.654
- [Beth] Oh, yeah.

00:08:24.654 --> 00:08:25.487
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:08:25.487 --> 00:08:26.364
(translates to Japanese)

00:08:26.364 --> 00:08:27.197
Wait, you do what?

00:08:27.197 --> 00:08:28.373
You say you love it while you do it?

00:08:28.373 --> 00:08:29.208
- [Beth] Yeah.

00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:30.288
(audience laughs)
- [Kelly] That's not weird.

00:08:30.288 --> 00:08:31.414
- [Translator] Make sure
you do it with love.

00:08:31.414 --> 00:08:32.247
(Marie speaks Japanese)

00:08:32.247 --> 00:08:33.080
- [Beth] I did something wrong.

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:33.913
- [Kelly] I love you.

00:08:33.913 --> 00:08:34.781
- [Beth] Oh, you're right.

00:08:34.781 --> 00:08:36.174
I've been doing it wrong.

00:08:36.174 --> 00:08:37.962
(Marie speaks Japanese)

00:08:37.962 --> 00:08:40.207
- [Translator] It's good
to make it a little skinny.

00:08:40.207 --> 00:08:41.040
- [Kelly] - [Beth] Okay.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:41.873
- [Kelly] Well.

00:08:41.873 --> 00:08:43.470
- [Beth] Your mom's like, "Well."

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:44.770
(laughs)

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:46.976
(speaks Japanese)

00:08:46.976 --> 00:08:49.635
- And then take the top,
